# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/packed-prefix development window (sticky sessions on the eight-seat 262k packed path;
# scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/packed-prefix and push a tag
# experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is
# pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-packed-prefix-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/packed-prefix commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# L1: the sticky-session LIFECYCLE on the audited arm (c2_prefix_gate.py --plan lifecycle, the PH4 of the design): lifecycle-evict then lifecycle-store (lifecycle-tiny is NOT_APPLICABLE on this profile: its pool is
# budgeted for every seat's whole context and the fast path has no preemption). lifecycle-evict: four arrivals at once, an abort while a request waits for a seat, an ABORT DURING A HIT'S PREFILL, a KV flood
# that evicts conversations built to ~56k (the coupled eviction: a hit after the flood restores less than before, with evicted_coupled on record), reset_prefix_cache, the KILL SWITCH file (grants off, latched, nothing
# published under it), an in-place restart (the first turn after it misses, the next hits). lifecycle-store: checkpoint LRU eviction. The KV RESERVATION is read on both (QWEN_FAST_KV_RESERVATION=1 in the profile):
# a request vLLM re-admitted (a second [PREFIX] row) is a FAIL (the fast path has no preemption), the hold lines and the hits restored are printed. The reservation's proof against vLLM's own scheduler with the prefix
# cache on is the CPU one (test_qwen_prefix_scheduler_vllm StickyReservationOnRealVllmTests, run by qwen-fast-vllm-cpu.yml): this job is the cards' half. READ: the plan verdict PASS, no pins held after
# every request ended, no commit mismatch, the 'KV reservation:' line with 0 re-admitted; the first FAIL or NOT_EXERCISED stops the window. Duration (estimate): 220 min. Stop rule.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-packed-prefix-1
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=lifecycle
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-prefix-gate
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best
